        "testata": "France 24",
        "lingua_originale": "en",
        "titolo_orig": "French heatwave drives up demand for AC, despite concerns",
        "testo_it": "Francia: l'ondata di caldo record fa impennare la richiesta di condizionatori d'aria in tutto il Paese.",
        "priorita": "Bassa",
        "id_gruppo": 6,
        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/french-heatwave-drives-up-demand-for-ac-despite-concerns",
        "orario": "15:20",
        "timestamp": 1782134427,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. French heatwave drives up demand for AC, despite concerns Europe Issued on: 22/06/2026 - 15:20 The second early-season heatwave of the year has brought the return of a politically-charged issue. That of air-conditioning - for decades, France has been notoriously reticent to adopt the technology - currently just 25% of French households have it. That figure is up significantly from just a decade ago, and it's set to keep rising as climate change brings increasingly frequent episodes of extreme heat. France's largely nuclear-based power generation means that the increased electricity consumption of AC has less of an environmental impact than elsewhere - but there are other concerns. 22/06/2026 Europe Change of UK PM likely 'a passing of the crown' while early general election unlikely 22/06/2026 Europe France struggles to deal with new heatwave amid punishing temperatures 22/06/2026 Europe Race starts to replace Keir Starmer as UK PM, with Burnham as favourite 22/06/2026 Europe Starmer resignation result of 'geopolitics' and shifting mood for 'flash and sparkle' 22/06/2026 Europe UK: PM Keir Starmer announces resignation 22/06/2026 Europe UK Prime Minister steps down: what to know 22/06/2026 Europe Replay: UK Prime Minister Keir Starmer steps down 22/06/2026 Europe 21/06/2026 Europe"
